1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,592
This is ThreatWeave, Stephen Butler's cybersecurity Graph RAG
project for CS sixty-three thirty-eight. This demonstration

2
00:00:08,592 --> 00:00:17,184
uses real saved application outputs from October fifteenth. It
makes no new model or database

3
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:24,630
calls. Synthetic narration accompanies captured application
states so the evidence workflow remains reproducible.

4
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:33,183
The question asks how Rhysida actors used valid accounts for
access and asks for separate

5
00:00:33,183 --> 00:00:40,485
mitigation guidance. The saved graph-only result identifies
compromised credentials used at internal VPN access points.

6
00:00:40,485 --> 00:00:47,787
Each claim lists the evidence identifiers supplied to the model.
The interface warns that a

7
00:00:47,787 --> 00:00:51,195
citation does not by itself establish correctness.

8
00:00:52,445 --> 00:01:00,233
Opening evidence E one reveals the exact CISA passage, its
advisory identifier and normalized source

9
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:08,021
offsets. Here the source explicitly connects Rhysida actors,
compromised valid credentials and internal VPN access.

10
00:01:08,021 --> 00:01:15,809
This lets the analyst check a particular incident observation
instead of assuming that a generally

11
00:01:15,809 --> 00:01:17,885
plausible answer is supported.

12
00:01:19,135 --> 00:01:26,232
Reference guidance has a different label. This passage comes from
the frozen Enterprise ATT and

13
00:01:26,232 --> 00:01:33,328
CK seventeen point one snapshot and describes secure handling of
credentials in applications. The relationship

14
00:01:33,328 --> 00:01:40,425
is a reference recommendation. It does not prove that this
mitigation worked against Rhysida in

15
00:01:40,425 --> 00:01:46,575
the reported incident. Keeping these source roles separate is a
core project requirement.

16
00:01:47,825 --> 00:01:55,483
The query graph displays the accepted directed paths actually
returned for this question. Selecting Valid

17
00:01:55,483 --> 00:02:03,141
Accounts exposes the technique identity and type. Actor-to-
technique and technique-to-mitigation links remain visible as
different

18
00:02:03,141 --> 00:02:10,799
relationships. The graph is a saved query-time snapshot rather
than a continuously refreshed picture of

19
00:02:10,799 --> 00:02:11,820
the database.

20
00:02:13,070 --> 00:02:19,956
The graph supports zoom, reset and panning. This captured state
follows the zoom-in control. These

21
00:02:19,956 --> 00:02:26,841
controls help inspect a returned path, but they do not validate
its meaning. The source

22
00:02:26,841 --> 00:02:33,726
passages remain necessary for checking whether the path supports
the wording of the generated answer.

23
00:02:34,976 --> 00:02:41,433
The sidebar can switch to the preserved full-hybrid run of the
same question. Full hybrid

24
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:47,891
combines text retrieval and structural paths with candidates
proposed by Node to Vec graph neighbors.

25
00:02:47,891 --> 00:02:54,348
The displayed answer and timestamp belong to that original run.
This replay is not a

26
00:02:54,348 --> 00:02:57,792
new performance measurement or a live benchmark query.

27
00:02:59,042 --> 00:03:07,301
The hybrid result also exposes its returned graph. Graph
similarity only proposes candidates. An accepted

28
00:03:07,301 --> 00:03:15,560
directed path with source evidence must support a factual claim.
The replay shows this distinction

29
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:23,819
without changing any frozen question, source, model output or
index. Additional live text-only and ablation

30
00:03:23,819 --> 00:03:26,022
interface flows remain unverified.

31
00:03:27,272 --> 00:03:35,613
Run details retain the model digest, evidence budget and
retrieval metadata. The actual evidence cap

32
00:03:35,613 --> 00:03:43,955
is three thousand UTF-eight bytes, even though the original
design discussed tokens. The download control

33
00:03:43,955 --> 00:03:52,297
exports the structured displayed run. Graph inspection can add
display-position metadata to entity records. The

34
00:03:52,297 --> 00:04:00,638
saved answer and evidence remain unchanged. Original pending-
review notices describe the October fifteenth development
checkpoint.

35
00:04:01,888 --> 00:04:10,109
The frozen evaluation contains twenty questions, four conditions
and three repeats, giving two hundred forty

36
00:04:10,109 --> 00:04:18,330
measured outcomes. Two hundred ten returned valid non-abstaining
answers, fifteen abstained and fifteen failed generation

37
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:26,552
validation. Valid here refers to output validation, not semantic
correctness. Automatic scoring retains missing and

38
00:04:26,552 --> 00:04:32,032
failed metric slots instead of filling them with invented values.

39
00:04:33,282 --> 00:04:40,278
Source-only extraction achieved precision zero point four five
five, recall zero point zero six seven

40
00:04:40,278 --> 00:04:47,274
and F one zero point one one seven against the frozen source-
scoped inventory. The proposed

41
00:04:47,274 --> 00:04:54,270
F one target of zero point eight was not met. Five exact-
reference nonmatches may expose

42
00:04:54,270 --> 00:05:01,266
annotation or granularity gaps, so disagreement with the
inventory is not always proof of semantic

43
00:05:01,266 --> 00:05:01,732
falsehood.

44
00:05:02,982 --> 00:05:10,972
ThreatWeave demonstrates a local workflow with cited answers,
exact source passages and inspectable graph paths.

45
00:05:10,972 --> 00:05:18,962
The preserved experiment, input hashes, validation failures and
scoring records make its limitations reviewable. The

46
00:05:18,962 --> 00:05:26,952
project does not establish operational effectiveness or a general
advantage for graph retrieval. The final

47
00:05:26,952 --> 00:05:32,811
report and slides provide the comparison results and their
coverage limitations.
